te0†Other Resources L7:   * cite0†My Subscriptions L8:   * cite0†My Favorites L9: \nL10: [Input]\nL11: \nL12: [Input]\nL13: \nL14:   * cite1†California Law >>\nL15:   * >>\nL16:   * Code Section\nL17: \nL18: [Input]\nL19: # Code Section\nL20: \nL21: [Input] Code:[Select]Article:[Input: I or II or XI]Section:[Input: 1 or 2 or 1001][Input] cite2†Image: information [Input]\nL22: \nL23: [Input] Code:[Select]Section: [Input]\nL24: Keyword(s):[Input][Input]\nL25: [Input]\nL26: \nL27: [Input]\nL28: \nL29: cite0†Code Search cite0†Text Search L30: \nL31: [Input]\nL32: \nL33: [Input] cite0†Up^ cite0†<< Previous cite0†Next >> cite0†cross-reference chaptered bills cite0†PDF | cite0†Add To My Favorites L34: [Input]\nL35: \nL36: [Input]\nL37: \nL38: Search Phrase: [Input][Input]\nL39: \nL40: [Input]\nL41: \nL42: [Input]\nL43: \nL44: #### Government Code - GOV\nL45: #### TITLE 2. GOVERNMENT OF THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA [8000 - 22980]\nL46: \nL47:   ( Title 2 enacted by Stats. 1943, Ch. 134. )\nL48: \nL49: \nL50: \nL51: #### DIVISION 3. EXECUTIVE DEPARTMENT [11000 - 15990.3]\nL52: \nL53:   ( Division 3 added by Stats. 1945, Ch. 111. )\nL54: \nL55: \nL56: \nL57: #### PART 1. STATE DEPARTMENTS AND AGENCIES [11000 - 11908]\nL58: \nL59:   ( Part 1 added by Stats. 1945, Ch. 111. )\nL60: \nL61: \nL62: \nL63: #### CHAPTER 3.5. Administrative Regulations and Rulemaking [11340 - 11361]\nL64: \nL65:   ( Heading of Chapter 3.5 amended by Stats. 1994, Ch. 1039, Sec. 2. )\nL66: ##### ARTICLE 3. Filing and Publication [11343 - 11343.8]\nL67: \nL68:   ( Article 3 added by Stats. 1979, Ch. 567. )\nL69: ###### 11343.\nL70: \nL71: Every state agency shall:\nL72: \nL73: (a) Transmit to the office for filing with the Secretary of State a certified copy of every regulation adopted or amended by it except one that is a building standard.\nL74: \nL75: (b) Transmit to the office for filing with the Secretary of State a certified copy of every order of repeal of a regulation required to be filed under subdivision (a).\nL76: (c) (1) Within 15 days of the office filing a state agency’s regulation with the Secretary of State, post the regulation on its internet website in an easily marked and identifiable location. The state agency shall keep the regulation on its internet website for at least six months from the date the regulation is filed with the Secretary of State.\nL77: (2) Within five days of posting, the state agency shall send to the office the internet website link of each regulation that the agency posts on its internet website pursuant to paragraph (1).\nL78: \nL79: (3) This subdivision shall not apply to a state agency that does not maintain an internet website.\nL80: \nL81: (d) Deliver to the office, at the time of transmittal for filing a regulation or order of repeal, a citation of the authority pursuant to which it or any part thereof was adopted.\nL82: (e) Deliver to the office a copy of the notice of proposed action required by Section 11346.4.\nL83: (f) Transmit to the California Building Standards Commission for approval a certified copy of every regulation, or order of repeal of a regulation, that is a building standard, together with a citation of authority pursuant to which it or any part thereof was adopted, a copy of the notice of proposed action required by Section 11346.4, and any other records prescribed by the California Building Standards Law (Part 2.5 (commencing with Section 18901) of Division 13 of the Health and Safety Code).\nL84: (g) Whenever a certification is required by this section, it shall be made by the head of the state agency that is adopting, amending, or repealing the regulation, or by a designee of the agency head, and the certification and delegation shall be in writing.\nL85: \nL86: (Amended by Stats. 2022, Ch. 48, Sec. 22. (SB 189) Effective June 30, 2022.)\nL87: \nL88: [Input]\n"
